{
  "summary": "The current `IDS_ROADIUM_SHIELDS_SITE_SCOPE` string incorrectly claims temporary exceptions only cover regular tabs. Analysis of `AdblockChromeContentBrowserClient::GetBrowserContextForEyeoFactories` confirms that the backend always returns the `GetOriginalProfile()`, meaning the filtering context is shared across both regular and private tabs. I recommend updating the help text to accurately reflect that exceptions apply to all views (including private tabs) and that other open tabs require a reload to apply changes.",
  "architecture_observations": [
    "`GetBrowserContextForEyeoFactories` remaps any context to the original profile, ensuring a shared filtering state.",
    "Private tabs (OffTheRecord) are not isolated from the adblock filtering logic.",
    "Temporary exceptions are stored in a separate memory vector on the original profile's configuration.",
    "UI controls only trigger reloads for the current tab; existing tabs remain in their previous state until reloaded."
  ],
  "proposed_changes": [
    {
      "file": "chrome/browser/adblock/android/adblock_strings.grd",
      "change": "Update `IDS_ROADIUM_SHIELDS_SITE_SCOPE` to include private tabs and clarify the reload requirement for other tabs."
    }
  ],
  "patch": "--- a/chrome/browser/adblock/android/adblock_strings.grd\n+++ b/chrome/browser/adblock/android/adblock_strings.grd\n@@ -215,7 +215,7 @@\n       <message name=\"IDS_ROADIUM_SHIELDS_SITE_PANEL_TITLE\" desc=\"Shields per-site panel: panel title\">Shields</message>\n-      <message name=\"IDS_ROADIUM_SHIELDS_SITE_SCOPE\" desc=\"Shields per-site panel: scope\">Applies to this host and its subdomains. Temporary exceptions cover regular tabs until the browser restarts. Closing a tab does not end the exception.</message>\n+      <message name=\"IDS_ROADIUM_SHIELDS_SITE_SCOPE\" desc=\"Shields per-site panel: scope\">Applies to this host and its subdomains. Temporary exceptions cover all tabs (including private) until the browser restarts. Other open tabs must be reloaded to apply changes. Closing a tab does not end the exception.</message>\n       <message name=\"IDS_ROADIUM_SHIELDS_SITE_GLOBAL_PAUSED\" desc=\"Shields per-site panel: global paused\">Protection is paused globally. Removing a site exception will not enable global protection.</message>",
  "risks": [
    "Minimal risk; this is a documentation/UI string correction."
  ],
  "tests": [
    "Verify the updated string appears correctly in the Shields per-site panel in the Android UI."
  ]
}
